WEBVTT

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.810
Feels great, huh?

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.940
No disagreement that it feels
great to be on this beach.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.940
But you haven't forgotten our original
purpose, have you, Siesta?

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.320
Purpose?

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.280
To get hold of the supposed "Emerald
Tear" and make some money?

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.370
Otherwise, we're flat bro--

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:44.540
Too bad. Since you failed to dodge,
you're now my servant for life, Kimi.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.340
Your penalties for being caught by
a surprise attack are too extreme.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.800
Here, hit it back.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.510
Is beach volleyball supposed
to be fun with just the two of us?

00:00:56.510 --> 00:01:00.390
You don't enjoy playing games with me?

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.680
No, it's not that.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.850
Then let's take a ride on that!

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:14.530
Are you seriously planning
not to row a single stroke?

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:18.700
I'm honoring the occasion since this
is your very first task as my servant.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:25.250
I feel like I'm always doing what you say,
irrespective of any game penalties.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.670
You're in surprisingly good shape.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:33.510
Cut it out.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.840
Nobody's looking.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:42.470
"If nobody's looking, it's okay"

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:42.470
is a skewed standard.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:49.560
You really aren't enjoying this?

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.110
It's not that...

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.740
I'm just realizing, when I think
about it, how far we've come.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:04.080
That day, we were in the air when I first
met you, and now it's been two years.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.080
Now we're on the ocean...

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:13.170
And? Are you enjoying yourself
now? Or are you not?

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:18.430
Hmm... I'll let you know when
this journey ends, someday.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:22.300
If that's your preference, that's fine.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.430
Oh, but if you're planning

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:26.770
to profess any feelings to me,
it'd be better to do it soon.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.810
Because I'm very sought-after.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.190
I wasn't planning to.
Also, stop bragging about yourself.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.190
Be that as it may...

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.570
Be <i>what </i>as it may?

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:39.530
Once we've gotten the jewel and eaten
tasty meat dishes to our heart's content,

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:42.700
shall we set up a detective
office somewhere?

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:47.370
That doesn't seem like any way
for an utterly broke person to talk.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.460
In this manner, our all-too-brief
summer vacation passed by,

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:57.920
and our absurd day-to-day life as
detective and sidekick recommenced.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.980
"Episode 5"
"That Was Directed
at One Year in the Future"

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:36.860
This is the work of Cerberus.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.270
Cerberus, you say?

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.860
That's an odd voice.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.570
I don't handle the smell of blood well.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:51.830
Maybe at least choose either to hunch
your neck or to plug your nose, not both?

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:58.000
So, this Cerberus is supposedly a Jack
the Ripper type who's recently emerged?

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:03.090
That's right: Codenamed Cerberus,
the guard dog of the underworld.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:06.680
The killer gobbles up
human hearts, they say.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.980
I was running late.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:16.270
There's no smoking here.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.230
Oh, then take this.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:23.240
It's time for my flight.
I'm headed back to Japan.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:29.280
What, already? I mean, what did you
come all the way here for, Fuubi-<i>san</i>?

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:33.330
A temporary transfer--although
that officially ended yesterday.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:36.460
I've never heard of that kind
of personnel transfer.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:40.250
For that reason, I'll leave the
legwork here to you two.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:44.260
Nab this modern-day second coming
of Jack the Ripper for us.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:47.010
Wait, but why?

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:54.180
Absurd. Why do I have to--?

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.020
What's that you've got?

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:59.400
Fuubi-<i>san </i>handed it over to me
just now when she left.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.820
Said she'd give it to me
because she was quitting smoking.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.780
I see. She handed over her
most valued possession

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:09.200
to a guy she was reconnecting
with after a long time.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:12.830
She handed over too much:
A half-smoked cigar, a lighter,

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:16.120
and a serial killer investigation...

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:19.000
So, what's the assailant's motive?

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:23.090
Why is Cerberus going around
poaching people's hearts?

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:27.840
It's hard to conceive of Cerberus
personally choosing to keep doing this.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:31.850
I believe these deeds are being
directed by a higher entity.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.600
Higher... from SPES?

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:38.560
Well, we can get the assailant to tell
us the motive after we catch them.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:41.520
Have you devised a way of doing that?

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:46.360
In fact, I was previously aware of
the ravages Cerberus was inflicting.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:51.240
Yeah, you wouldn't ever let a case as
extreme as this escape your attention.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.580
The assailant seems to have a great nose.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:58.210
Try as I might to get close, the killer
has slipped away again and again.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:04.960
Bat has his ear, so Cerberus could be
an android with a reconstructed nose.

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:11.800
But now, for some reason,
regardless of our being in town,

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.180
Cerberus is still committing these crimes.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.640
A trap?

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.020
I meant to say this is our big chance.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:24.190
You may say so, but how, specifically,
do we go about the pursuit?

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:28.610
You've got it backwards.
We're not going to pursue Cerberus.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:31.990
Cerberus is going to come after us.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:38.370
You can't possibly be planning
to use me as a decoy?

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.830
Your deduction skills
have really improved.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:45.840
So how about we work out
the plan over afternoon tea?

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.010
You're the only human being in the world

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:52.220
who can go straight from a
murder scene to afternoon tea.

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:56.680
More to the point, before we came here
weren't you gorging on Sunday roast?

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.560
I'm constantly exhausting my brain,

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.980
so my three basic cravings are somewhat
stronger than other people's.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:05.400
Is that why you're always napping?

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:09.610
You're one to talk, Mr. Morning Sluggard.

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:13.610
Your <i>three </i>basic cravings
are stronger than others'...

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:19.750
My mistake: I only meant food and sleep.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:27.090
It'll soon be three years since we began
traveling the world together, Kimi.

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:29.460
Feels like the blink of
an eye somehow, huh?

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:32.760
Don't suddenly get all
nostalgic about the past.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:36.600
You are going to come save me
before I get murdered, right?

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:42.430
Sidekick or no, I don't intend
to offer up my life.

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:48.320
So... I wonder if Cerberus is really
going to come to this room.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.400
Not to worry. If I've read
the situation right,

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.740
you'll be devoured by Cerberus tonight.

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:57.280
So I'm just going to be murdered?

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:01.160
Honestly, I don't know if today
will be the day or not.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:04.330
I guess that's true. We're only
saying it's more probable

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.210
that Cerberus will target me
when I'm separated from you.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:09.550
I do have a plan, for what it's worth,

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:13.420
so whenever you're attacked, there's
a 1 in 10,000 chance you'll survive.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:19.430
So I have only a 1 in 10,000
chance of survival, eh?

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:21.680
I can't come near you,

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:26.810
but I'll at least stay on the phone
with you, so you're not lonely.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:59.930
Hate to say it, but I'm used to being
on the verge of being killed.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:04.060
Hey! Stop jumping to conclusions!

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:13.860
Char! Why are you...?

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:18.280
Ah, I see. Siesta asked you to be here?

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:24.370
That's right! Seriously, using all your
might to hurl a girl onto a bed...

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:27.120
Where'd you learn to behave like that?

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:31.670
If you're going to harp on that, isn't it
beyond threatening to sneak into a room

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:34.800
with the lights off
and approach without a word?

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.170
That's because, you know,

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:40.220
there was a possibility that Cerberus
might've gotten here ahead of me.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:47.100
Even so, Siesta could've told me
if she was asking you to help.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:51.060
Keeping things under wraps
is part of Siesta's strategy, right?

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:55.530
What?

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:58.650
Who are you?

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:02.490
Char doesn't ever refer
to Siesta by her name.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:07.580
I see. So I've been found out.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:19.420
You've got that kind of ability?

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:25.140
It's a full moon tonight.
My blood is crying out.

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:37.900
I'll take that heart.

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:40.360
So you're Cerberus.

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:56.040
You are way too packed.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:20.820
I have to buy myself time somehow...

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:25.070
Hmm...? You seem to handle yourself well.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:29.040
I thought you were just the
legendary detective's flunky,

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.660
but I'll have to alter that assessment.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:38.090
Why are you doing all this?
What's your purpose?

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:42.880
I have no motive. I'm only carrying
out my assigned mission.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:47.180
Killing you is also part of that mission.

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:48.890
Prepare yourself!

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:51.560
"Siesta"

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:52.770
Get down.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:12.660
Took you long enough to come.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:17.380
I got here in time, so it's fine,
right? Did you miss me?

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:26.590
I couldn't sense your presence with
the acuity of this nose... why is that?

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:32.930
I think it's because, up until a moment
ago, this room was full of a special gas.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.690
Gas?

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:37.350
It can't be...

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:41.820
She anticipated this would happen
and rigged gas to supplement the water?

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:45.780
As a result, Cerberus's sense
of smell was incapacitated...

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:49.120
As usual, you've taken
preparation to extremes.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:53.040
I had faith that you'd
definitely do just what you did.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:58.750
And with that, I win. Time to accept that.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:02.800
I can't... be apprehended yet.

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:07.090
It's no use.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.140
Sidekick!

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:14.770
You're not getting away!

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:18.900
This is absurd!

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:28.610
I have a mission. One more...
We have to acquire one more living heart!

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:31.580
In that case, you can just leave yours.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:42.960
Sidekick!

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:45.760
Be careful.

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:50.760
It's our first time actually meeting
face to face like this, isn't it...

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.850
...Legendary Detective?

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.180
Who are you?

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:03.610
My name is Hel. Codename... Hel.

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.820
Codename... so she's also...

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:13.370
She's SPES's supreme leader.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.450
Well, now...

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:35.100
With this, the last of the parts
have been gathered.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:37.890
Now to take this back
and execute the pla--

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:40.140
You think I'll allow you to put
your plan into action?

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:45.480
You won't be able to fire.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:47.320
What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.080
Siesta!

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:02.460
Well... shall we go and see
the netherworld together?

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:14.600
Where am I?

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:23.310
Looks like you're awake.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.980
Hel...

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:30.860
How are you feeling? Not in pain anywhere?

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:34.740
Hard to believe those are
the words of an abductor.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:38.740
I think it's only natural to be
concerned about a partner.

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:41.870
I'm your partner?
I don't follow what that means.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:45.250
How could doing such a
thing possibly benefit you?

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:47.710
You have a low opinion of yourself.

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:50.010
Call it modesty.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.680
You're capable of laughing, too, eh?

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:59.930
What do you think I am?
I'm just a normal girl, after all.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:05.190
I don't believe a normal girl could kill
a compatriot like that, though.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:11.280
Compatriot? No, he was no more than a cog
for the purpose of executing a plan.

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:14.820
Do you intend to use and
discard me in that way, too?

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:17.530
I wouldn't do anything like that.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:18.950
Still...

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:24.790
...what's inscribed in
the Sacred Writ is absolute.

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:26.830
The Sacred Writ?

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:30.500
Have you ever heard of
the Leaves of Agastya?

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.210
I seem to recall something

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:35.800
about a prophetic scripture written before
the common era by a certain sage.

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:41.770
That's right. This Sacred Writ originated
with the Leaves of Agastya as its basis.

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:45.940
And your future, too, has been
set down in these pages.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.190
Your eyes show you don't
believe a word I'm saying.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:56.780
Yeah, but don't fret about that. There's
only one person I trust besides myself.

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:04.330
So you were a magnet for trouble...
That's your nature...

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:07.670
Why do you know that?

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:12.170
But I believe your nature is
a little different from that.

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:16.970
You're not a magnet for trouble.
You bring out trouble in the world.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.890
What are you talking about?

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:23.970
Your... <i>That</i>... is an ability to cause
changes in things, to provoke incidents.

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:28.940
You yourself are a pivot point
for the world. Therefore...

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:36.990
I'm going to have you become my partner.
In order to save the world with me.

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:39.410
You misspoke--you mean
to destroy the world.

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:42.530
To me, that would be salvation.

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:49.540
Well, according to the Sacred Writ, your
joining me will apparently come later.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:53.420
Still, having things move
quickly is Father's--

00:18:56.470 --> 00:19:02.600
It's unfortunate, though. There'd be
a lot of perks in partnering with me.

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:07.350
So, what do you say, Kimi?

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:09.940
Become my partner.

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:13.320
Right, of course...

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:19.610
...I refuse. Even you didn't actually
believe I'd take that hand.

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:20.950
Was it that obvious?

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:26.700
Well, instead, there's something
I'd like you to see.

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:34.040
This.

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:38.170
What... is that?

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:40.380
It's a biological weapon.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:47.640
This fella can exhale a special breath
that contains some toxins.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:50.770
You mean to use it to engage
in some sort of terrorism?

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.560
Exactly.

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:59.490
On that note, I never answered
your question about where we are.

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:04.660
It's an underground facility directly
beneath this nation's Parliament building.

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:10.250
So if you were able to set up such a site
in a nation's nucleus of power,

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:14.040
I must be safe in assuming you've
got some powerful collaborators.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:19.050
And? Do you mean to release that
thing in the city to feed on people?

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:23.890
No, that's not it. We've given
it plenty of provisions.

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:28.640
Given it provisions... So that's it...

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:35.650
That monster eats human hearts... They're
its provisions, or its power source.

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:38.780
You truly do have good intuition.

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:45.120
Petelgeuse... time to go to work.

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:00.420
By all means I want you,
who will become my partner someday,

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:03.220
to see what comes next for yourself.

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:04.470
No.

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:09.060
You're going to be stopped, here and now.

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:13.890
How? What on Earth can you do,
without even a weapon...?

00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:17.020
When did I say <i>I'd </i>stop you?

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:29.450
Sidekick! Sidekick, where are you?

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:32.370
Sidekick! Where are you, Sidekick?

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:38.630
Come on, Sidekick! Are you not here?
Sidekick... Sidekick!

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:45.220
This wall is in the way. Who needs it?
I'll take the whole thing out!

00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:10.870
You are the most burdensome sidekick ever.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:14.160
Your "it's whatever" act
towards me isn't convincing.

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:50.010
"Episode 6"
"Crimson Devil, Ice Queen"
